-- AB-LENGTH-RETRY-1 (2026-10-19, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 100277, recurrence of the closed 100167): doctrine bookkeeping for qnfo-model-eval 1.8.0.
-- The worker change: abOneFixture asks a post-change reply that is empty AND finished with "length" once more, at Math.min(4096, Math.max(2048, 4 x the fixture budget)),
-- through the same path (router pinned, then the Workers AI id), and never after the run deadline. An empty reply with any other finish stays an immediate loss; a model that is
-- still empty at the larger budget still loses ("empty post-change reply (finish length) after retry at N tokens"); a retry that cannot be made (call error, a reply from another
-- model, the deadline) leaves the fixture unmeasured, which is neither a loss nor callFailed. abPersist writes harness_rev (AB_HARNESS_REV, now 2) as the FIRST key of
-- model_ab_runs.detail, and abAlreadyRun counts a 'regression' row as done only when its detail starts with the current revision, so a regression scored by the older harness is
-- measured again. No model_ab_runs row is edited or deleted: ids 1 and 4 stay as history. Two further decisions of the hourly tick (the reason for the minor release):
--   * abStaleRevCandidates is a third candidate source next to the policy file and ai_call_counters: every worker, pre and post model with a 'regression' row from the last 10080 minutes
--     whose detail does not start with the current harness_rev prefix is proposed (source 'stale-rev'), whether or not ai_call_counters still shows a model change. ab_max_runs_per_tick (2),
--     ab_daily_cap (12) and abAlreadyRun bound it, and a pair stops being proposed once it has a row of the current revision.
--   * abAlreadyRun no longer counts an inconclusive row whose skipped fixtures say "retry unavailable" as done: it counts with the error rows, so such a pair is tried again on the next
--     tick and rests for the rest of the day after 3 of them. Other inconclusive rows (no independent judge family, judges that disagree) keep their 10080-minute dedupe.
--
-- WHY (read 2026-10-20 from qnfo-audit, SELECT only):
--   * model_ab_runs id 1 (qnfo-research-exec) and id 4 (errata-hub), the same pair (glm-5.3-flash -> kimi-k2.6, grounded-qa), 0 wins, 4 ties, 4 losses, win rate 0.25 both times, below the 0.40 line.
--     All four losses of run 4 (gq-3, gq-5, gq-6, gq-8) and two of the four of run 1 (gq-3, gq-8) are "empty post-change reply (finish length)"; the other two losses of run 1 (gq-4, gq-6)
--     are judged answers and real. With the empties out, run 4 has 4 valid items against a minimum of 6: inconclusive, not a regression. Issue 100167 (run 1) was closed on 2026-10-19 with that
--     finding at 15:11Z, and the same artifact filed 100277 (run 4) at 23:24Z, so the root cause (the harness) was never fixed.
--   * The fixtures cap max_tokens at 200 to 400 (grounded-qa 300) and the call carries no thinking switch, so a reasoning model (scripts/model-policy.json allowed[].reasoning true) can spend the
--     whole cap on thought and return empty text with finish length. That is the harness budget and not the model's answer. The production call differs: the errata-hub confirm step
--     (qnfo-research-exec CONFIRM_MODEL_OTHER = kimi-k2.6) sends max_tokens 2048, temperature 0 and chat_template_kwargs thinking false, and ai_call_counters for errata-hub on 2026-10-19 reads
--     kimi-k2.6 20 calls, 0 errors, 1676 output tokens (about 84 a call, a short JSON verdict), glm-5.3-flash 24 calls, 0 errors. The worker the harness flagged runs a different task under different
--     settings. The retry floor is 2048 tokens, the production confirm budget, and no model-specific switch is added.
--   * abAlreadyRun deduped a pair on any non-error row for 10080 minutes, so after a harness fix the stale regression rows (ids 1 and 4) would have suppressed the re-run until 2026-10-26 and 100277 would have
--     stayed open with nothing probing it. Fixing only that dedupe is not enough, because the ai_call_counters source is a window that closes by itself. abObservedCandidates' own statement, run read-only
--     on 2026-10-20 with ab_min_calls 20, returns exactly two pairs: errata-hub/kimi-k2.6 (35 calls in the last two days, none before) and q08-signal-engine/gpt-oss-20b (already inconclusive as id 5, so deduped).
--     qnfo-research-exec/kimi-k2.6 is NOT a candidate any more: its 223 calls on 2026-10-18 count as prior once the date rolled at 00:00Z 2026-10-20 (the rule needs fewer than 3), so that pair left the window
--     before this file merged; issue 100167 was closed on the finding that research-exec no longer uses kimi-k2.6 as its primary model. scripts/model-policy.json names no workers and model_ab_policy_seen
--     is empty, so the policy source adds nothing. The errata-hub window closes the same way at 00:00Z 2026-10-21, when its 20 calls of 2026-10-19 become prior. POST /ab/run needs the x-eval-key, which no
--     session holds. Without the stale-rev source the id 1 pair would never be measured again, the errata-hub pair would depend on a deploy landing before 2026-10-21 00:00Z, and a first re-run that came out
--     inconclusive (kimi errors are common: AB-HARNESS-1 recorded 282 errors in 547 research-exec kimi calls) would end the only chance. With it both pairs are proposed from their stored rows until those rows are
--     10080 minutes old (id 1 at 14:21Z and id 4 at 23:24Z on 2026-10-26), or until each has a row of the current revision.
--   * The remediation contract of issue 100277 is born superseded with the circular placeholder probe (it observes the issue's own status), so nothing probes the defect. The issue text names the real
--     probe (the newest model_ab_runs verdict for the worker and post model is pass) only in prose.
--
-- WHAT THIS FILE CHANGES
--   remediation_contracts  issue-100277: the circular placeholder is replaced (the row is copied to bak_20261019_issue_100277_contract first) by a probe that cannot pass before a fixed run exists: expected 'pass',
--                          observed the verdict of the newest model_ab_runs row for errata-hub and kimi-k2.6 whose detail starts with the harness_rev 2 prefix when that verdict is pass or regression, and
--                          'pending: ...' when there is no such row or the newest one is inconclusive or error (a run that reached no verdict; a deferral by the fleet's convention, never a pass and never a failure,
--                          and the tick measures the pair again). Active, d1-query, like the issue-2828 replacement in 2026-10-19-model-ab.sql. The statement changes nothing when the
--                          issue is not open, the contract is absent, or the contract no longer holds the placeholder. This file writes nothing to agent_issues or issue_triage: the issue closes through its contract
--                          after a real rev-2 run passes.
--   failure_modes          ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss with its standing detector contract fm-ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss (d1-query): rows of a harness revision that carries harness_rev, written in the last
--                          120 minutes, holding a length-empty loss that was not retried (the item text ends right after "finish length)"). It reads 0 on the fixed harness, where a retried loss reads
--                          "finish length) after retry at N tokens", and 1 if the retry is ever bypassed. The window is 120 minutes, the ceiling of SLA-120M-1, and the contract is read hourly, so every
--                          row is read at least once. model_ab_runs rows are history and are never edited, so a longer window would latch the contract at 1 after a code fix that no data repair could
--                          clear, and the issue it raises could not close inside the 120-minute issue SLA (SLA-120M-2); with this window the read clears by itself 120 minutes after the last bad row.
--   control_registry       model-ab-run-cap and model-ab-switch (DOCTRINE-1 section 16): this change alters both controls, so their registry text is corrected, both rows stay 'keep'. The cap's evidence
--                          said a run is at most 24 calls and 12 runs a day at most 288, and its alternate path said an unrun pair is detected again only while the change is inside the ai_call_counters
--                          window; the switch's evidence said the dedupe on worker, pre and post model is the same for every row. The rows are copied to bak_20261019_model_ab_controls first, each UPDATE is
--                          guarded by the sentence it replaces (a replay, or a row already edited by hand, is left alone), and the Rollback restores the three columns from the copy. A rest of 3 runs
--                          a day for a pair whose retries stay unavailable is a new cap-like rest; it is recorded in the cap's evidence and alternate path.
--   decision_log           one row (append-only), with a prediction decision_predictions_parse reads.
-- Cost: a run was at most 8 post-change and 16 judge calls (24); a length-empty fixture adds one retry call, so at most 32, and ab_daily_cap (12 runs) bounds a day at 384 calls against 288. The retry runs inside the existing
-- AB_RUN_BUDGET_MS deadline, and a pair whose retries stay unavailable costs at most 3 runs a day (96 calls) inside that cap. model-ab-run-cap bounds runs, but its registry evidence did its call arithmetic
-- with the old 24, so the two control_registry rows are corrected here (see WHAT THIS FILE CHANGES): the cap and the switch stay 'keep' with the same alternate path, and their text states 32 and 384, the stale-rev source and the
-- revision-gated dedupe. A registry that records a belief the change made false is a false belief on the scorecard (control_registry, DOCTRINE-1 section 16).
-- Prediction: the metric model_ab_judged_runs_7d (pass or regression runs in the last 7 days) reads 4 on 2026-10-20 (ids 1 to 4; id 5, q08-signal-engine at 04:20Z, is inconclusive and not counted). Both stale pairs are proposed by
-- the next hourly tick (errata-hub by the ai_call_counters source and the stale-rev source, qnfo-research-exec by the stale-rev source alone) and both fit in ab_max_runs_per_tick (2), so the metric reaches 6 once both re-runs reach a
-- verdict. A pair that stays inconclusive (fewer than 6 measured fixtures, judges that disagree) leaves it at 5 or 4 and the prediction misses; that is the honest reading of a pair the harness cannot measure. The window is 4 h: one
-- hourly tick, the hourly metric refresh, and a second chance for a pair whose retries were unavailable.
-- decision_log is append-only (trigger decision_log_no_delete), so the Rollback leaves the decision row; replaying this file changes nothing (every statement is guarded or INSERT OR IGNORE on the row key).
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE remediation_contracts SET (precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, status, last_verdict, module, attempts) = (SELECT precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, status, last_verdict, module, attempts FROM bak_20261019_issue_100277_contract) WHERE class = 'issue-100277' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bak_20261019_issue_100277_contract); UPDATE control_registry SET (alternate_path, evidence, reviewed_at) = (SELECT b.alternate_path, b.evidence, b.reviewed_at FROM bak_20261019_model_ab_controls b WHERE b.control = control_registry.control) WHERE control IN ('model-ab-run-cap', 'model-ab-switch') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bak_20261019_model_ab_controls b WHERE b.control = control_registry.control); DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'fm-ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss'; DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key = 'ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss'

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261019_issue_100277_contract AS
SELECT class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, status, last_verdict, module, attempts, next_due_at FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'issue-100277';

UPDATE remediation_contracts SET
  precondition = 'AB-LENGTH-RETRY-1 (qnfo-model-eval 1.8.0, migrations/2026-10-19-ab-length-retry.sql)',
  action = 'the errata-hub kimi-k2.6 pair is measured again by the fixed A/B harness: the newest model_ab_runs row for the worker and post model whose detail starts with harness_rev 2 reads pass; a run that reached no verdict (inconclusive or error) reads pending and the hourly tick measures the pair again; the placeholder this replaces read only the issue''s own status',
  verify_transport = 'd1-query',
  verify_probe = 'SELECT ''pass'' AS expected, CASE (SELECT verdict FROM model_ab_runs WHERE worker = ''errata-hub'' AND post_model = ''@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6'' AND detail LIKE ''{"harness_rev":2,%'' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) WHEN ''pass'' THEN ''pass'' WHEN ''regression'' THEN ''regression'' ELSE ''pending: the newest errata-hub run on kimi-k2.6 of the fixed harness revision is missing or reached no verdict (inconclusive or error)'' END AS observed',
  module = 'issue-100277-ab-length-retry',
  status = 'active',
  last_verdict = NULL,
  attempts = 0,
  next_due_at = datetime('now')
WHERE class = 'issue-100277' AND issue_id = 100277
  AND instr(verify_probe, 'FROM agent_issues WHERE id = 100277') > 0
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = 100277 AND status = 'open');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO failure_modes (fm_key, failure_mode, root_cause, remediation, detector, probe_class, first_seen, issue_id, trigger_condition, symptom, blast_radius)
VALUES ('ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss',
  'an A/B run scores a post-change reply that is empty only because the fixture''s own token cap was spent as a loss, so a reasoning model regresses on the harness budget and the same false regression is filed again after its issue was closed',
  'abOneFixture scored an empty reply as a loss without looking at its finish reason. The fixtures cap max_tokens at 200 to 400 and send no thinking switch, so a reasoning model (kimi-k2.6) spends the whole cap on thought and returns empty text with finish length. Read 2026-10-20: model_ab_runs id 1 (qnfo-research-exec) and id 4 (errata-hub), the same pair, win rate 0.25 both times; all four losses of run 4 and two of the four of run 1 were "empty post-change reply (finish length)", while the production errata-hub confirm call sends thinking false at 2048 tokens and answers in about 84 output tokens. Issue 100167 was closed on the symptom and 100277 is the recurrence. A second cause: abAlreadyRun deduped a regression row on worker, pre and post model for 10080 minutes whatever scoring wrote it, and the only source of candidates was a window of ai_call_counters that closes by itself (qnfo-research-exec kimi-k2.6 left it on 2026-10-20, errata-hub kimi-k2.6 leaves it on 2026-10-21), so a harness fix could not re-measure the stale pairs.',
  'qnfo-model-eval 1.8.0 AB-LENGTH-RETRY-1: a length-empty reply is asked once more at Math.min(4096, Math.max(2048, 4 x the fixture budget)) through the same path and never after the run deadline; a retry that cannot be made leaves the fixture unmeasured and not a loss; a model still empty at the larger budget still loses with "after retry at N tokens" in the item. AB_HARNESS_REV 2 leads every model_ab_runs.detail and abAlreadyRun counts a regression row as done only at the current revision, while abStaleRevCandidates proposes every pair whose regression row of the last 10080 minutes is of an older revision, so the hourly tick re-runs it without an ai_call_counters window; an inconclusive run that lost fixtures to an unavailable retry is tried again, at most 3 times a day. Closing probe: contract issue-100277 (newest rev-2 errata-hub kimi-k2.6 verdict is pass).',
  'no model_ab_runs row that carries harness_rev, written in the last 120 minutes, holds a length-empty loss that was not retried (detail contains finish length) followed by a closing quote; a retried loss reads finish length) after retry at N tokens); the 120-minute window is the SLA ceiling, so the read clears by itself 120 minutes after the last bad row; contract fm-ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss',
  'fm-ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss', '2026-10-19', 100277,
  'a post-change model that spends its whole output budget on reasoning (finish length) at a fixture budget of 200 to 400 tokens',
  'MODEL-AB-REGRESSION-1 issues with a win rate of 0.25 whose losing items all read "empty post-change reply (finish length)"',
  'the model-quality signal for every reasoning model (kimi-k2.6 today) and one false high issue per pair (100167 and 100277 in one day)');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, escalate_to, expected_cadence_h, status, module, budget_ms, max_items, requires_container, next_due_at)
VALUES ('fm-ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss', NULL, 'AB-LENGTH-RETRY-1', 'failure mode detector',
  'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM model_ab_runs WHERE detail LIKE ''{"harness_rev":%'' AND instr(detail, ''finish length)"'') > 0 AND created_at >= datetime(''now'', ''-120 minutes'')) AS TEXT) AS observed',
  'd1-query', 3, 'qnfo-fleet-control', 1, 'active', 'failure-mode', 45000, 5, 0, datetime('now'));

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261019_model_ab_controls AS
SELECT * FROM control_registry WHERE control IN ('model-ab-run-cap', 'model-ab-switch');

UPDATE control_registry SET
  evidence = 'MEASURED 2026-10-19: three observed model changes in the last two days (qnfo-research-exec, qnfo-code-orchestrator, qnfo-fleet-control); at most 2 runs a tick drains them in two ticks. REVISED 2026-10-20 (AB-LENGTH-RETRY-1, qnfo-model-eval 1.8.0): a run is at most 32 calls (8 post-change, up to 8 retries of a length-empty reply at a larger budget, 16 judge), so 12 runs a day is at most 384 calls through qnfo-ai; before the retry it was 24 and 288. The stale-rev candidate source needs no ai_call_counters window: every pair with a regression row of an older harness revision from the last 10080 minutes is proposed on each tick until it has a row of the current revision, inside ab_max_runs_per_tick and ab_daily_cap. An inconclusive run whose skipped fixtures say "retry unavailable" counts with the error rows, so the pair is tried again on the next tick and rests after 3 such rows in a day (at most 96 calls for that pair). A cadence cap, not a spend budget: a breached ai_spend cap does not skip a run (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1).',
  alternate_path = 'raise ab_max_runs_per_tick or ab_daily_cap in cf_model_eval_config, or run POST /ab/run by hand for one pair; unrun candidates are detected again on the next tick from the policy file, from the ai_call_counters window (the current and the previous day of counters, which closes by itself) and, since qnfo-model-eval 1.8.0, from the stale-rev source, which proposes a pair whose regression row of the last 10080 minutes was scored by an older harness revision and needs no ai_call_counters window; a pair whose retries stay unavailable is tried again on each tick and rests after 3 such runs in a day',
  reviewed_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
WHERE control = 'model-ab-run-cap' AND instr(evidence, 'A run is at most 24 calls') > 0;

UPDATE control_registry SET
  evidence = replace(evidence, 'dedupe on worker, pre and post model for 7 days', 'dedupe on worker, pre and post model for 10080 minutes, revision-gated for regression rows since qnfo-model-eval 1.8.0 (a regression row counts as done only when its detail starts with the current harness_rev, so one scored by an older harness is measured again; an inconclusive row whose skipped fixtures say "retry unavailable" is not deduped but counts with the error rows and rests the pair after 3 in a day)'),
  reviewed_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
WHERE control = 'model-ab-switch' AND instr(evidence, 'dedupe on worker, pre and post model for 7 days') > 0;

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'session_01QpQv19uh1padRwZ3u1r766',
 'an empty reply with finish length is the harness budget and not an answer, so scoring it as a loss measures the fixture''s token cap and the retry at a larger budget measures the model; a regression row written by an older scoring is not evidence about the current harness',
 'AB-LENGTH-RETRY-1: qnfo-model-eval 1.8.0 asks a length-empty post-change reply once more at Math.min(4096, Math.max(2048, 4 x the fixture budget)) through the same path and never after the run deadline, leaves a fixture whose retry cannot be made unmeasured, writes harness_rev 2 first in model_ab_runs.detail so abAlreadyRun counts a regression row only at the current revision, proposes every pair whose regression row of the last 10080 minutes is of an older revision (abStaleRevCandidates, source stale-rev, no ai_call_counters window needed) and tries an inconclusive run that lost fixtures to an unavailable retry again, at most 3 times a day; migrations/2026-10-19-ab-length-retry.sql replaces the circular superseded contract of issue 100277 with a probe on the newest rev-2 errata-hub kimi-k2.6 verdict (an inconclusive or error run reads pending), adds the failure mode ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss with its detector fm-ab-length-empty-scored-as-loss (a 120-minute window, so one bad row cannot hold the contract at 1 past the SLA ceiling), and corrects the control_registry rows model-ab-run-cap (32 calls a run and 384 a day, the stale-rev source needs no ai_call_counters window, the rest of 3 runs a day for a pair whose retries stay unavailable) and model-ab-switch (the dedupe is revision-gated for regression rows), both still keep',
 'qnfo-audit 2026-10-20, SELECT only: model_ab_runs ids 1 and 4 (same pair, win rate 0.25, 4 ties and 4 losses each; the losses of run 4 and two of run 1 are empty replies with finish length at a 300-token fixture); ai_call_counters errata-hub 2026-10-19 kimi-k2.6 20 calls, 0 errors, 1676 output tokens, and 15 calls on 2026-10-20; abObservedCandidates'' own statement (ab_min_calls 20) returns only errata-hub/kimi-k2.6 (35 recent calls, none before) and q08-signal-engine/gpt-oss-20b (inconclusive id 5, deduped), and not qnfo-research-exec/kimi-k2.6, whose 223 calls on 2026-10-18 count as prior since 00:00Z 2026-10-20 (issue 100167 closed on the finding that research-exec no longer uses kimi-k2.6 as primary); model_ab_policy_seen has no rows and scripts/model-policy.json names no workers; contract issue-100277 superseded with the circular placeholder; the production confirm call is thinking off at 2048 tokens; control_registry read live 2026-10-20: model-ab-run-cap evidence still states a run of at most 24 calls and 288 a day and ties re-detection of an unrun pair to the ai_call_counters window, model-ab-switch evidence states the dedupe without the revision gate, and neither control has a control_alternate_probes row',
 'pending',
 'qnfo-model-eval only: at most one extra call per fixture, on a length-empty reply only (a run is at most 32 calls against 24, 12 runs a day at most 384 against 288, a pair whose retries stay unavailable at most 3 runs a day inside that cap); no route, binding, table schema or model choice changes (the only existing rows rewritten are the evidence, alternate_path and reviewed_at of control_registry model-ab-run-cap and model-ab-switch, copied first to bak_20261019_model_ab_controls); no model_ab_runs row is edited or deleted; the next hourly tick re-runs both stale regression pairs (errata-hub, also found by the ai_call_counters window that closes at 00:00Z 2026-10-21, and qnfo-research-exec, which left that window at 00:00Z 2026-10-20 and is proposed from its stored row only), glm-5.3-flash to kimi-k2.6, until each has a row of the current revision or its stale row is 10080 minutes old (2026-10-26)',
 'revert qnfo-model-eval 1.8.0 through the canonical path (rows written at revision 2 stay as history), or the Rollback header: it restores the issue-100277 contract from bak_20261019_issue_100277_contract, restores the evidence, alternate_path and reviewed_at of the two control_registry rows from bak_20261019_model_ab_controls and removes the failure mode and its detector (decision_log is append-only and keeps this row); cf_model_eval_config ab_enabled = 0 stops the tick within one tick',
 'the A/B harness measures a reasoning model''s answers and not the fixture''s token cap, a regression found by an older scoring is measured again by the hourly tick without a manual run or a live ai_call_counters window (POST /ab/run needs the x-eval-key, which no session holds), and a run the harness could not complete is tried again instead of ending the only chance',
